  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1991-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(a=2^x-4\\) and \\(b=4^x-2.\\) The right side is \\((a+b)^3,\\) so \\[ a^3+b^3=(a+b)^3 \\] is equivalent to \\(ab(a+b)=0.\\) The cases give \\(2^x=4,\\) \\(4^x=2,\\) or \\(4^x+2^x=6,\\) whose real solutions are \\(x=2,\\frac12,\\) and \\(1,\\) respectively. Their sum is \\(2+\\frac12+1=\\frac72.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Set \\(a=2^x-4\\) and \\(b=4^x-2\\)",
        "Factor \\(a^3+b^3-(a+b)^3\\) as \\(-3ab(a+b)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
